1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,080
What's Today's Video About? Let's Talk About the Reason!

2
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:09,580
Scene 1: Conversation Before the Rain

3
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:13,220
Wow, the sky looks so dark.

4
00:00:13,243 --> 00:00:15,221
It really does.

5
00:00:15,244 --> 00:00:18,644
There are so many dark clouds.

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:21,236
It's going to rain soon.

7
00:00:21,259 --> 00:00:22,625
Yeah.

8
00:00:22,648 --> 00:00:25,015
Do you have an umbrella?

9
00:00:25,038 --> 00:00:27,723
No, I don’t.

10
00:00:27,747 --> 00:00:31,113
Then, share mine.

11
00:00:31,136 --> 00:00:33,221
Thank you.

12
00:00:33,244 --> 00:00:37,878
It's okay, I have a big one.

13
00:00:37,902 --> 00:00:39,950
That’s so kind of you.

14
00:00:39,973 --> 00:00:42,866
Oh, no, not at all.

15
00:00:42,889 --> 00:00:46,622
Oh, the wind is getting stronger too.

16
00:00:46,645 --> 00:00:48,887
It sure is.

17
00:00:48,911 --> 00:00:51,247
It’s getting cold.

18
00:00:51,270 --> 00:00:53,046
Let’s hurry.

19
00:00:53,070 --> 00:00:55,727
Yeah, let’s do that.

20
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,022
Should we run to the station?

21
00:00:58,046 --> 00:01:01,324
It’s dangerous, so let’s walk.

22
00:01:01,347 --> 00:01:03,080
Alright.

23
00:01:03,103 --> 00:01:06,636
Oh, it’s starting to rain.

24
00:01:06,659 --> 00:01:09,326
Let’s open the umbrella quickly.

25
00:01:09,349 --> 00:01:11,082
Please.

26
00:01:11,105 --> 00:01:13,706
Are your things okay?

27
00:01:13,730 --> 00:01:18,063
My bag might get wet, so I’ll hold it in front.

28
00:01:18,086 --> 00:01:20,130
I can carry it for you.

29
00:01:20,154 --> 00:01:22,087
It’s okay.

30
00:01:22,110 --> 00:01:24,077
Alright then.

31
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:27,834
Oh, I hear thunder.

32
00:01:27,857 --> 00:01:29,823
That’s scary.

33
00:01:29,846 --> 00:01:33,302
Should we go into a nearby café?

34
00:01:33,326 --> 00:01:34,959
That sounds good.

35
00:01:34,982 --> 00:01:38,982
The rain is heavy, so let’s take a break.

36
00:01:39,005 --> 00:01:42,606
There’s a new café around that corner.

37
00:01:42,629 --> 00:01:44,363
Over there?

38
00:01:44,386 --> 00:01:46,596
Yes, let’s go.

39
00:01:46,619 --> 00:01:55,628
You can download today’s video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

40
00:01:55,628 --> 00:01:57,128
Scene 2: Choosing Clothes and Comparing Prices

41
00:01:57,128 --> 00:02:00,168
How about this outfit?

42
00:02:00,192 --> 00:02:02,458
That sounds good.

43
00:02:02,481 --> 00:02:06,966
We have a red shirt and a blue shirt.

44
00:02:06,990 --> 00:02:09,590
Which one do you like?

45
00:02:09,613 --> 00:02:13,979
I like the red shirt.

46
00:02:14,002 --> 00:02:16,569
It looks great on you!

47
00:02:16,592 --> 00:02:18,662
Thank you.

48
00:02:18,686 --> 00:02:21,019
Are you going to buy it?

49
00:02:21,042 --> 00:02:25,775
It’s a bit expensive, so I’m not sure.

50
00:02:25,798 --> 00:02:27,599
How much is it?

51
00:02:27,622 --> 00:02:30,092
It’s 5,000 yen.

52
00:02:30,116 --> 00:02:33,082
That’s a bit pricey.

53
00:02:33,105 --> 00:02:37,379
The blue shirt is 3,000 yen.

54
00:02:37,403 --> 00:02:39,271
That's cheap!

55
00:02:39,295 --> 00:02:40,928
Yeah.

56
00:02:40,951 --> 00:02:45,320
But the red shirt is cuter.

57
00:02:45,344 --> 00:02:48,177
I think so too.

58
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:51,835
Then let's go with the red shirt.

59
00:02:51,858 --> 00:02:56,346
But I don't have enough money to buy it.

60
00:02:56,370 --> 00:02:58,403
Want me to lend you some?

61
00:02:58,426 --> 00:03:01,159
Really? Are you sure?

62
00:03:01,182 --> 00:03:04,618
Yeah, it's no problem.

63
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:06,409
I'm sorry about this.

64
00:03:06,432 --> 00:03:08,665
Don't worry about it.

65
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:12,359
I'll definitely pay you back next month.

66
00:03:12,383 --> 00:03:14,949
Take your time.

67
00:03:14,972 --> 00:03:16,739
Thank you.

68
00:03:16,762 --> 00:03:20,377
Is there anything else you want?

69
00:03:20,401 --> 00:03:25,620
My shoes are old, so I'd like new ones.

70
00:03:25,644 --> 00:03:27,977
Want to check out the shoe store too?

71
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,733
Yes, I'd love to.

72
00:03:30,756 --> 00:03:34,489
There's a big shoe store over there.

73
00:03:34,512 --> 00:03:36,389
Let's go!

74
00:03:36,413 --> 00:03:43,518
You can review today's video with the link in the description and top comment. *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

75
00:03:43,518 --> 00:03:45,018
Scene 3: Inviting to a Movie and Declining

76
00:03:45,018 --> 00:03:48,452
Are you free this Saturday?

77
00:03:48,475 --> 00:03:50,678
This Saturday?

78
00:03:50,702 --> 00:03:52,271
Yeah.

79
00:03:52,294 --> 00:03:54,311
Do you have plans?

80
00:03:54,334 --> 00:03:58,192
I got two movie tickets.

81
00:03:58,216 --> 00:04:00,185
A movie?

82
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:02,042
Yeah.

83
00:04:02,066 --> 00:04:05,236
It's a new action film.

84
00:04:05,260 --> 00:04:07,066
That sounds good.

85
00:04:07,089 --> 00:04:10,531
Want to go see it with me?

86
00:04:10,554 --> 00:04:15,554
I'd love to, but Saturday is a bit tough.

87
00:04:15,577 --> 00:04:17,511
Alright then.

88
00:04:17,534 --> 00:04:21,348
I have a part-time job, so I can't go.

89
00:04:21,371 --> 00:04:23,971
Until what time?

90
00:04:23,994 --> 00:04:26,927
Until 8 PM.

91
00:04:26,950 --> 00:04:29,529
That's too bad.

92
00:04:29,552 --> 00:04:32,288
I'm really sorry.

93
00:04:32,312 --> 00:04:35,045
How about Sunday?

94
00:04:35,068 --> 00:04:38,201
Sunday is my day off.

95
00:04:38,224 --> 00:04:41,500
Then let's go on Sunday.

96
00:04:41,524 --> 00:04:45,207
Are the tickets for Saturday?

97
00:04:45,231 --> 00:04:49,270
No, they work for any day.

98
00:04:49,294 --> 00:04:51,494
Alright then.

99
00:04:51,517 --> 00:04:54,950
How about 1 PM on Sunday?

100
00:04:54,973 --> 00:04:57,976
That time works for me.

101
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,633
Great!

102
00:05:00,656 --> 00:05:03,099
I'm looking forward to it.

103
00:05:03,122 --> 00:05:06,764
Want to grab a bite after the movie?

104
00:05:06,788 --> 00:05:08,755
That sounds good.

105
00:05:08,778 --> 00:05:14,421
I know a great Italian place—let's go there.

106
00:05:14,444 --> 00:05:16,778
I'd love that!

107
00:05:16,801 --> 00:05:21,810
Then let's meet at the station at 12:30 on Sunday.

108
00:05:21,833 --> 00:05:23,800
Alright.

109
00:05:23,823 --> 00:05:26,429
Don't be late, okay?

110
00:05:26,452 --> 00:05:28,385
It’s okay.

111
00:05:28,408 --> 00:05:29,908
Scene 4: Reasons for Being Late and Apologies

112
00:05:29,908 --> 00:05:32,342
You're late.

113
00:05:32,365 --> 00:05:35,765
Sorry I'm late.

114
00:05:35,788 --> 00:05:38,086
What happened?

115
00:05:38,109 --> 00:05:43,743
The roads were so jammed, the bus couldn't move.

116
00:05:43,767 --> 00:05:45,767
Was there an accident?

117
00:05:45,790 --> 00:05:49,723
Yes, there was a bad one.

118
00:05:49,746 --> 00:05:52,679
That must have been rough.

119
00:05:52,702 --> 00:05:55,472
I'm really sorry.

120
00:05:55,495 --> 00:05:58,529
I’ve been waiting forever.

121
00:05:58,552 --> 00:06:00,752
Were you cold?

122
00:06:00,775 --> 00:06:03,872
A little.

123
00:06:03,895 --> 00:06:07,062
Let’s grab something warm to drink.

124
00:06:07,085 --> 00:06:08,852
Thank you.

125
00:06:08,875 --> 00:06:11,041
Coffee okay?

126
00:06:11,064 --> 00:06:15,997
I’d love some tea, if that’s alright.

127
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:17,867
Alright.

128
00:06:17,891 --> 00:06:21,299
There’s a vending machine over there.

129
00:06:21,323 --> 00:06:23,222
I’ll go get it.

130
00:06:23,245 --> 00:06:25,492
I’ll wait here.

131
00:06:25,516 --> 00:06:27,982
Here’s your tea.

132
00:06:28,005 --> 00:06:29,772
Thank you.

133
00:06:29,795 --> 00:06:32,852
What time does the movie start?

134
00:06:32,875 --> 00:06:37,327
We’ve still got 30 minutes—we’ll make it.

135
00:06:37,351 --> 00:06:39,524
We’ll be on time!

136
00:06:39,548 --> 00:06:42,127
Phew, what a relief.

137
00:06:42,150 --> 00:06:45,550
I’ll leave earlier next time.

138
00:06:45,573 --> 00:06:48,573
Yeah, give yourself some extra time.

139
00:06:48,596 --> 00:06:50,366
I will.

140
00:06:50,389 --> 00:06:53,756
Alright, let’s head to the theater.

141
00:06:53,779 --> 00:06:56,517
Yes, let’s go.

142
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:59,073
Do you have the tickets?

143
00:06:59,096 --> 00:07:02,363
Yep, they’re in my bag.

144
00:07:02,386 --> 00:07:04,794
Great!

145
00:07:04,818 --> 00:07:06,318
Scene 5: Reporting Sickness

146
00:07:06,318 --> 00:07:09,328
Hello, good morning.

147
00:07:09,351 --> 00:07:11,641
Good morning.

148
00:07:11,665 --> 00:07:13,515
I'm sorry about this.

149
00:07:13,538 --> 00:07:16,829
I won’t be able to come to school today.

150
00:07:16,853 --> 00:07:18,819
What happened?

151
00:07:18,842 --> 00:07:24,642
I’ve had a terrible headache since this morning—I can’t even get up.

152
00:07:24,665 --> 00:07:27,147
Do you have a fever?

153
00:07:27,171 --> 00:07:30,405
Yes, I’ve got a 38°C fever.

154
00:07:30,428 --> 00:07:33,312
That’s pretty high.

155
00:07:33,335 --> 00:07:35,946
My throat hurts too.

156
00:07:35,970 --> 00:07:38,261
Are you going to the hospital?

157
00:07:38,284 --> 00:07:41,818
Yes, I’ll go this afternoon.

158
00:07:41,841 --> 00:07:45,641
Could be the flu.

159
00:07:45,664 --> 00:07:47,430
Not sure yet.

160
00:07:47,453 --> 00:07:49,908
Have you taken any medicine?

161
00:07:49,931 --> 00:07:55,627
I haven’t been to the hospital yet, so I don’t have any prescription meds.

162
00:07:55,651 --> 00:07:57,784
Alright then.

163
00:07:57,807 --> 00:08:00,505
I took some over-the-counter stuff.

164
00:08:00,529 --> 00:08:03,699
You should get some rest.

165
00:08:03,722 --> 00:08:06,156
I will.

166
00:08:06,179 --> 00:08:09,179
What about today’s test?

167
00:08:09,202 --> 00:08:11,735
I’ll call the teacher.

168
00:08:11,758 --> 00:08:15,034
Want me to let the teacher know?

169
00:08:15,058 --> 00:08:16,698
Please.

170
00:08:16,721 --> 00:08:19,209
No, I’ve got it.

171
00:08:19,233 --> 00:08:21,234
Thank you.

172
00:08:21,257 --> 00:08:23,824
Just take it easy.

173
00:08:23,847 --> 00:08:26,783
I might be out tomorrow too.

174
00:08:26,806 --> 00:08:29,865
Please take it easy.

175
00:08:29,888 --> 00:08:31,778
That’s so kind of you.

176
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:34,881
Get well soon.

177
00:08:34,904 --> 00:08:37,159
Yes, thank you.

178
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:40,023
See you tomorrow.

179
00:08:40,046 --> 00:08:42,129
Excuse me.

180
00:08:42,153 --> 00:08:43,653
Scene 6: Time-Saving Transportation / Beat the Clock with Smart Commute Choices

181
00:08:43,653 --> 00:08:46,304
It's already eight o'clock.

182
00:08:46,328 --> 00:08:49,261
Yeah, let's hurry.

183
00:08:49,284 --> 00:08:52,418
How do you usually get to the office?

184
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:55,207
I usually take the train.

185
00:08:55,230 --> 00:08:58,499
Should we walk to the station now?

186
00:08:58,523 --> 00:09:02,990
It's too far to walk—it'll take too long.

187
00:09:03,013 --> 00:09:05,222
What about the bus?

188
00:09:05,246 --> 00:09:08,379
The bus will take too long too.

189
00:09:08,402 --> 00:09:12,675
We're short on time, so let's take a taxi.

190
00:09:12,699 --> 00:09:14,266
It sure is.

191
00:09:14,289 --> 00:09:16,922
Should I call one?

192
00:09:16,945 --> 00:09:19,552
There's a taxi right over there.

193
00:09:19,576 --> 00:09:21,448
Let's wave it down.

194
00:09:21,471 --> 00:09:23,838
It stopped!

195
00:09:23,861 --> 00:09:25,327
Let's get in.

196
00:09:25,350 --> 00:09:28,384
Oh, the door opened.

197
00:09:28,407 --> 00:09:30,540
To the office, please.

198
00:09:30,563 --> 00:09:32,649
Will we make it in time?

199
00:09:32,672 --> 00:09:36,246
The roads are clear, so we should be fine.

200
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:38,003
Great!

201
00:09:38,026 --> 00:09:41,193
What time do you usually leave home?

202
00:09:41,216 --> 00:09:43,226
I leave at seven.

203
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:45,783
Did you oversleep today?

204
00:09:45,806 --> 00:09:47,289
Yeah.

205
00:09:47,312 --> 00:09:50,512
I stayed up late last night.

206
00:09:50,535 --> 00:09:52,869
What were you doing?

207
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:55,309
Watching a movie.

208
00:09:55,333 --> 00:09:57,425
Was it good?

209
00:09:57,448 --> 00:10:02,332
It was so good I watched it all the way through.

210
00:10:02,356 --> 00:10:04,646
Make sure to go to bed early tonight.

211
00:10:04,670 --> 00:10:07,036
I will.

212
00:10:07,059 --> 00:10:10,326
Oh, we're almost at the office.

213
00:10:10,349 --> 00:10:12,435
That was fast!

214
00:10:12,459 --> 00:10:15,145
Taxis are so convenient.

215
00:10:15,168 --> 00:10:16,668
Scene 7: Curry Crawl / Picking the Perfect Curry Spot for a Flavorful Walk

216
00:10:16,668 --> 00:10:19,739
I'm starving.

217
00:10:19,763 --> 00:10:22,897
Yeah, let's grab something to eat.

218
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:25,287
What are you in the mood for?

219
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:28,944
I'm craving curry.

220
00:10:28,967 --> 00:10:32,033
Curry? Sounds great.

221
00:10:32,056 --> 00:10:36,456
I love spicy food, so I eat it all the time.

222
00:10:36,479 --> 00:10:39,285
Which place should we go to?

223
00:10:39,309 --> 00:10:44,042
There's a new Indian restaurant in front of the station.

224
00:10:44,065 --> 00:10:47,798
Is their curry good?

225
00:10:47,821 --> 00:10:51,036
My friend said it's delicious.

226
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:53,027
Let's check it out.

227
00:10:53,050 --> 00:10:55,816
Should we walk?

228
00:10:55,839 --> 00:10:58,573
It's close, so let's walk.

229
00:10:58,596 --> 00:11:01,996
There are so many options on the menu!

230
00:11:02,019 --> 00:11:05,152
I'll go with the chicken curry.

231
00:11:05,175 --> 00:11:08,822
I'll have the vegetable curry.

232
00:11:08,845 --> 00:11:11,618
What would you like to drink?

233
00:11:11,642 --> 00:11:15,893
It's spicy, so I'd like some cold water.

234
00:11:15,916 --> 00:11:19,650
I'll have a sweet juice.

235
00:11:19,673 --> 00:11:25,206
According to my friend, the naan here is delicious too!

236
00:11:25,229 --> 00:11:28,429
Then let's order some naan as well.

237
00:11:28,452 --> 00:11:31,319
Would you like some rice too?

238
00:11:31,343 --> 00:11:36,110
I'm really hungry, so I'll have rice too.

239
00:11:36,133 --> 00:11:38,333
You're going to eat a lot, huh?

240
00:11:38,356 --> 00:11:41,956
Yeah, I love eating.

241
00:11:41,979 --> 00:11:44,579
Same here.

242
00:11:44,602 --> 00:11:46,970
Here comes the food!

243
00:11:46,993 --> 00:11:48,770
Let's dig in!

244
00:11:48,793 --> 00:11:51,467
This is really delicious!

245
00:11:51,491 --> 00:11:54,624
Yeah, let's come again.

246
00:11:54,647 --> 00:11:58,344
Next time, I want to try a different curry.

247
00:11:58,368 --> 00:12:00,376
It sure is.

248
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,900
Scene 8: Weekend Tennis – Stay Active and Have Fun!

249
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:05,666
What do you do on weekends?

250
00:12:05,689 --> 00:12:07,823
I play tennis.

251
00:12:07,845 --> 00:12:10,891
Do you play tennis every week?

252
00:12:10,914 --> 00:12:15,085
Yes, I go every Sunday.

253
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:17,392
Do you like tennis?

254
00:12:17,416 --> 00:12:21,582
I love it—it's so much fun!

255
00:12:21,605 --> 00:12:24,296
Where do you play tennis?

256
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:27,853
There’s a court at the nearby park.

257
00:12:27,876 --> 00:12:30,409
Who do you play with?

258
00:12:30,432 --> 00:12:32,968
I play with my friends.

259
00:12:32,991 --> 00:12:35,325
That sounds good.

260
00:12:35,348 --> 00:12:39,791
Sports are great—they help relieve stress.

261
00:12:39,814 --> 00:12:43,581
I want to try a sport too.

262
00:12:43,604 --> 00:12:47,137
Do you have a favorite sport?

263
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:50,727
I love swimming.

264
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:53,716
How about going to the pool?

265
00:12:53,739 --> 00:12:58,237
It's winter now, so the water is cold.

266
00:12:58,261 --> 00:13:01,027
There’s an indoor pool, though.

267
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:03,490
That sounds nice!

268
00:13:03,514 --> 00:13:07,354
It’s warm and feels great.

269
00:13:07,377 --> 00:13:10,581
I’ll go to the pool on my next day off.

270
00:13:10,605 --> 00:13:12,971
Are you going alone?

271
00:13:12,994 --> 00:13:15,733
I’ll go with my sister.

272
00:13:15,757 --> 00:13:19,230
Does your sister like swimming too?

273
00:13:19,254 --> 00:13:25,820
Yes, she’s taking lessons and is really good at it.

274
00:13:25,843 --> 00:13:28,058
That’s wonderful!

275
00:13:28,082 --> 00:13:32,701
After swimming, I always eat something delicious.

276
00:13:32,724 --> 00:13:35,324
What do you eat?

277
00:13:35,347 --> 00:13:38,313
I have warm ramen.

278
00:13:38,336 --> 00:13:42,342
Ramen is perfect when you're hungry.

279
00:13:42,366 --> 00:13:46,139
Yeah, I’m looking forward to the weekend!

280
00:13:46,163 --> 00:13:47,663
Scene 9: Learning Japanese and Future Dreams – Unlock New Opportunities!

281
00:13:47,663 --> 00:13:51,429
How's your Japanese study going?

282
00:13:51,452 --> 00:13:56,252
Kanji is tough, so it's challenging.

283
00:13:56,275 --> 00:13:59,209
Are you studying every day?

284
00:13:59,232 --> 00:14:03,867
I study for two hours every day.

285
00:14:03,890 --> 00:14:06,262
That's impressive!

286
00:14:06,285 --> 00:14:11,118
I want to work at a Japanese company, so I'm pushing myself.

287
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:14,159
What kind of company do you want to join?

288
00:14:14,183 --> 00:14:17,383
I want to work at a car company.

289
00:14:17,406 --> 00:14:20,372
Do you like Japanese cars?

290
00:14:20,395 --> 00:14:23,929
They're so cool—I love them!

291
00:14:23,952 --> 00:14:28,233
Do you plan to live in Japan in the future?

292
00:14:28,256 --> 00:14:32,856
Yes, Japan is safe, so I'd love to live there long-term.

293
00:14:32,879 --> 00:14:35,617
The food is delicious too!

294
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:38,974
I love sushi and ramen.

295
00:14:38,997 --> 00:14:42,164
What do you do on your days off?

296
00:14:42,187 --> 00:14:45,253
I watch Japanese anime.

297
00:14:45,276 --> 00:14:48,510
Do you study Japanese through anime?

298
00:14:48,533 --> 00:14:52,899
It's fun, so it's a great way to learn.

299
00:14:52,922 --> 00:14:56,889
How about going to see a movie together sometime?

300
00:14:56,913 --> 00:14:59,208
What movie?

301
00:14:59,231 --> 00:15:02,898
It's a new anime film.

302
00:15:02,921 --> 00:15:04,654
I'd love that!

303
00:15:04,677 --> 00:15:06,844
I'd love to go!

304
00:15:06,867 --> 00:15:11,600
It'll be good Japanese practice, so let's chat a lot.

305
00:15:11,623 --> 00:15:13,592
Thank you.

306
00:15:13,616 --> 00:15:17,849
If there's anything you don't understand, just ask.

307
00:15:17,872 --> 00:15:21,872
I'll bring a dictionary, so no worries.

308
00:15:21,895 --> 00:15:23,628
Alright then.

309
00:15:23,651 --> 00:15:25,500
That's really dedicated of you!

310
00:15:25,523 --> 00:15:30,523
I have a test next week, so I'll study even more.

311
00:15:30,546 --> 00:15:32,746
I'm rooting for you!

312
00:15:32,769 --> 00:15:35,036
Thank you.

313
00:15:35,059 --> 00:15:36,559
Scene 10: Planning a Summer Trip

314
00:15:36,559 --> 00:15:41,159
Are you going on a trip for summer vacation?

315
00:15:41,182 --> 00:15:44,787
Yes, I'd love to go somewhere.

316
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:47,010
Where do you want to go?

317
00:15:47,033 --> 00:15:50,768
I'd like to go to the mountains or the beach.

318
00:15:50,792 --> 00:15:53,192
Which do you prefer?

319
00:15:53,215 --> 00:15:58,066
It's so hot, so I'd rather go somewhere cool like the mountains.

320
00:15:58,089 --> 00:16:00,023
That sounds good.

321
00:16:00,046 --> 00:16:02,879
How about Hokkaido?

322
00:16:02,902 --> 00:16:08,478
Hokkaido is far, so flights would be expensive.

323
00:16:08,501 --> 00:16:11,668
Then how about Hakone?

324
00:16:11,691 --> 00:16:14,709
Hakone sounds great!

325
00:16:14,733 --> 00:16:19,500
There are hot springs, so you can relax.

326
00:16:19,524 --> 00:16:25,891
I want to soak in an onsen, so let's book that hotel I saw online earlier.

327
00:16:25,914 --> 00:16:28,347
Which hotel?

328
00:16:28,370 --> 00:16:32,587
It's an old hotel in the mountains.

329
00:16:32,611 --> 00:16:34,944
Isn't it expensive?

330
00:16:34,967 --> 00:16:39,235
It's cheap if we book online.

331
00:16:39,258 --> 00:16:41,692
That sounds nice!

332
00:16:41,715 --> 00:16:45,153
I heard the food is delicious too!

333
00:16:45,177 --> 00:16:48,033
What kind of food do they serve?

334
00:16:48,056 --> 00:16:52,691
I heard they serve a lot of fish dishes.

335
00:16:52,714 --> 00:16:56,997
I love fish, so that makes me happy!

336
00:16:57,021 --> 00:16:59,354
When do you want to go?

337
00:16:59,377 --> 00:17:03,115
Let's leave on the 5th of next month.

338
00:17:03,138 --> 00:17:05,272
For three days?

339
00:17:05,295 --> 00:17:09,742
Since we don’t have much time off, it’ll be two days.

340
00:17:09,765 --> 00:17:12,032
Got it.

341
00:17:12,055 --> 00:17:15,121
Should I buy the train tickets too?

342
00:17:15,144 --> 00:17:18,923
It’ll be crowded, so let’s buy them early.

343
00:17:18,947 --> 00:17:21,434
I’ll buy them at the station today.

344
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:23,391
Please.

345
00:17:23,414 --> 00:17:26,682
I can’t wait for the trip!

346
00:17:26,705 --> 00:17:30,197
I’m really looking forward to it too!

347
00:17:30,221 --> 00:17:31,721
Scene 11: Handling a Lost Passport

348
00:17:31,721 --> 00:17:34,121
What happened?

349
00:17:34,144 --> 00:17:37,436
I can’t find my passport.

350
00:17:37,459 --> 00:17:40,459
What? Really?

351
00:17:40,482 --> 00:17:44,731
Yeah, it’s not in my bag.

352
00:17:44,755 --> 00:17:47,488
How about your pockets?

353
00:17:47,511 --> 00:17:50,409
I checked my pockets too.

354
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:52,713
But it’s not there.

355
00:17:52,736 --> 00:17:55,474
Where did you lose it?

356
00:17:55,498 --> 00:17:57,746
Not sure yet.

357
00:17:57,770 --> 00:18:01,003
Where did you go today?

358
00:18:01,026 --> 00:18:03,793
I went to the bank.

359
00:18:03,816 --> 00:18:06,902
Where did you go after that?

360
00:18:06,926 --> 00:18:10,326
I did some shopping at the department store.

361
00:18:10,349 --> 00:18:14,515
Did you use the restroom there?

362
00:18:14,538 --> 00:18:17,738
Yes, I did.

363
00:18:17,761 --> 00:18:21,328
You might’ve left it there.

364
00:18:21,351 --> 00:18:23,484
It sure is.

365
00:18:23,507 --> 00:18:26,907
Should I call the department store?

366
00:18:26,930 --> 00:18:29,764
Yes, please.

367
00:18:29,786 --> 00:18:31,786
Hello?

368
00:18:31,809 --> 00:18:35,696
Have you found any lost passports?

369
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,199
I see...

370
00:18:38,223 --> 00:18:39,990
Alright.

371
00:18:40,013 --> 00:18:42,086
Did they find it?

372
00:18:42,109 --> 00:18:44,920
No, they haven’t.

373
00:18:44,944 --> 00:18:47,119
This is bad.

374
00:18:47,142 --> 00:18:50,309
I’m supposed to go back home the day after tomorrow.

375
00:18:50,332 --> 00:18:53,108
That’s a big problem.

376
00:18:53,131 --> 00:18:55,931
Should we go to the police?

377
00:18:55,954 --> 00:18:57,388
It sure is.

378
00:18:57,411 --> 00:18:59,883
I’ll go with you.

379
00:18:59,906 --> 00:19:01,873
I'm sorry about this.

380
00:19:01,896 --> 00:19:03,729
Thank you.

381
00:19:03,752 --> 00:19:06,919
Oh, wait a minute.

382
00:19:06,942 --> 00:19:09,142
What happened?

383
00:19:09,165 --> 00:19:13,498
Your coat pocket looks a little bulky.

384
00:19:13,521 --> 00:19:16,254
Oh, you’re right!

385
00:19:16,277 --> 00:19:18,519
Oh! Here it is!

386
00:19:18,542 --> 00:19:20,309
It’s my passport!

387
00:19:20,332 --> 00:19:23,827
It was in your coat pocket all along.

388
00:19:23,851 --> 00:19:27,884
Yes, I’m so sorry.

389
00:19:27,907 --> 00:19:29,684
Great!

390
00:19:29,708 --> 00:19:31,641
I’m so relieved.

391
00:19:31,664 --> 00:19:33,164
Scene 12: Invitation to an Izakaya

392
00:19:33,164 --> 00:19:37,807
Are you free this Friday?

393
00:19:37,831 --> 00:19:41,664
Friday? At night?

394
00:19:41,687 --> 00:19:45,620
Yeah, after work.

395
00:19:45,643 --> 00:19:48,477
Is something going on?

396
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:53,304
We’re all going to check out a new izakaya.

397
00:19:53,327 --> 00:19:55,527
That sounds good.

398
00:19:55,550 --> 00:19:58,124
Would you like to go together?

399
00:19:58,148 --> 00:20:04,514
I'd love to, but I have plans this Friday.

400
00:20:04,537 --> 00:20:08,548
I see. Working overtime?

401
00:20:08,572 --> 00:20:13,405
No, my mom is coming over.

402
00:20:13,428 --> 00:20:15,527
Your mom?

403
00:20:15,551 --> 00:20:20,353
Yes, she's visiting from the countryside.

404
00:20:20,377 --> 00:20:23,270
That sounds fun!

405
00:20:23,293 --> 00:20:28,060
Yeah, we're going to have dinner together.

406
00:20:28,083 --> 00:20:31,887
So Friday won't work, huh?

407
00:20:31,911 --> 00:20:35,077
I'm really sorry.

408
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:37,702
Don't worry about it.

409
00:20:37,726 --> 00:20:40,696
Please invite me again next time!

410
00:20:40,719 --> 00:20:43,157
How about Saturday?

411
00:20:43,181 --> 00:20:49,181
I'm going shopping with my mom on Saturday.

412
00:20:49,204 --> 00:20:51,637
How about Sunday?

413
00:20:51,660 --> 00:20:57,393
Sunday works—I'll see my mom off then.

414
00:20:57,416 --> 00:21:02,183
Then how about going to see a movie on Sunday?

415
00:21:02,206 --> 00:21:04,648
A movie?

416
00:21:04,672 --> 00:21:08,441
There's a really interesting one playing.

417
00:21:08,464 --> 00:21:11,797
Sounds great! Let's go.

418
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:15,688
Let's plan for Sunday afternoon, then.

419
00:21:15,711 --> 00:21:17,645
Alright.

420
00:21:17,668 --> 00:21:20,334
I'm looking forward to it.

421
00:21:20,357 --> 00:21:24,524
Enjoy your meal with your mom!

422
00:21:24,547 --> 00:21:26,837
Thank you.

423
00:21:26,861 --> 00:21:28,361
Scene 13: Reporting a Late Arrival

424
00:21:28,361 --> 00:21:31,966
Hello, good morning.

425
00:21:31,990 --> 00:21:34,356
Good morning.

426
00:21:34,379 --> 00:21:36,913
Where are you now?

427
00:21:36,936 --> 00:21:40,169
I'm at the station.

428
00:21:40,192 --> 00:21:43,968
Work is about to start soon.

429
00:21:43,991 --> 00:21:48,258
Sorry, I'll be a little late.

430
00:21:48,281 --> 00:21:50,737
What happened?

431
00:21:50,760 --> 00:21:56,374
The train was delayed, so I'll be about 10 minutes late.

432
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:58,431
Was there an accident?

433
00:21:58,454 --> 00:22:04,787
Yes, there was a big accident, so the trains stopped.

434
00:22:04,810 --> 00:22:08,777
That's rough.

435
00:22:08,800 --> 00:22:12,167
I'm heading there by taxi now.

436
00:22:12,190 --> 00:22:15,860
The taxis are probably packed too.

437
00:22:15,884 --> 00:22:22,051
There are so many people in front of the station—I might not even get a ride.

438
00:22:22,074 --> 00:22:25,013
I'll walk from the station.

439
00:22:25,036 --> 00:22:28,203
Don't push yourself too hard.

440
00:22:28,226 --> 00:22:30,792
And don't run, okay?

441
00:22:30,815 --> 00:22:34,187
Got it, I'll be careful.

442
00:22:34,211 --> 00:22:37,030
What time does the meeting start?

443
00:22:37,054 --> 00:22:42,787
The meeting starts at 10, so you'll be fine.

444
00:22:42,810 --> 00:22:45,044
Great!

445
00:22:45,067 --> 00:22:46,700
I’m so relieved.

446
00:22:46,723 --> 00:22:49,941
No need to rush.

447
00:22:49,965 --> 00:22:53,022
I'm really sorry about this.

448
00:22:53,045 --> 00:22:57,724
It's not your fault, so don't worry about it.

449
00:22:57,747 --> 00:22:59,480
Thank you.

450
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:03,042
Please be careful on your way here.

451
00:23:03,066 --> 00:23:06,843
Okay, I'll get there as soon as I can.

452
00:23:06,867 --> 00:23:10,300
Let me know when you arrive at the office.

453
00:23:10,323 --> 00:23:12,739
Alright.

454
00:23:12,763 --> 00:23:15,059
Will do, thanks.

455
00:23:15,083 --> 00:23:18,049
Alright, I'll be waiting.

456
00:23:18,072 --> 00:23:20,407
Excuse me.

457
00:23:20,431 --> 00:23:21,931
Scene 14: Reporting Illness

458
00:23:21,931 --> 00:23:24,331
Good morning.

459
00:23:24,354 --> 00:23:26,687
Good morning.

460
00:23:26,710 --> 00:23:28,677
What's wrong?

461
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:31,507
Your voice sounds off.

462
00:23:31,530 --> 00:23:38,930
I actually have a fever of 38°C, so I'll be taking the day off today.

463
00:23:38,953 --> 00:23:41,638
Thirty-eight degrees, huh?

464
00:23:41,662 --> 00:23:44,307
That’s pretty high.

465
00:23:44,331 --> 00:23:50,427
Yes, I have a bit of a cough too, and my throat hurts.

466
00:23:50,450 --> 00:23:53,322
Have you been to the hospital yet?

467
00:23:53,346 --> 00:23:56,913
I'm heading there now.

468
00:23:56,936 --> 00:24:00,903
Is there a hospital nearby?

469
00:24:00,926 --> 00:24:06,597
There's a new one in front of the station, so I'll go there.

470
00:24:06,620 --> 00:24:09,257
That's good to hear.

471
00:24:09,281 --> 00:24:11,779
Can you eat anything?

472
00:24:11,802 --> 00:24:16,889
I have no appetite, so I haven't eaten anything yet.

473
00:24:16,913 --> 00:24:20,479
You should drink some soup or something.

474
00:24:20,502 --> 00:24:24,116
Okay, I'll have just a little.

475
00:24:24,140 --> 00:24:28,673
About this afternoon's meeting—can I cancel it?

476
00:24:28,696 --> 00:24:30,630
It’s okay.

477
00:24:30,653 --> 00:24:35,859
I'll contact the client for you, so don't worry.

478
00:24:35,883 --> 00:24:37,816
Thank you.

479
00:24:37,839 --> 00:24:40,039
That would be a huge help.

480
00:24:40,062 --> 00:24:42,835
Where are the documents?

481
00:24:42,859 --> 00:24:47,862
They're on my desk—go ahead and check them.

482
00:24:47,885 --> 00:24:49,852
Alright.

483
00:24:49,875 --> 00:24:51,521
I'll take a look.

484
00:24:51,545 --> 00:24:56,545
I'm really sorry for all the trouble.

485
00:24:56,568 --> 00:25:01,866
Your health is the most important thing, so make sure to rest.

486
00:25:01,889 --> 00:25:03,541
Thank you.

487
00:25:03,564 --> 00:25:08,220
Take your medicine and get plenty of sleep, okay?

488
00:25:08,244 --> 00:25:10,537
I will.

489
00:25:10,561 --> 00:25:13,295
Do you think you'll be able to come in tomorrow?

490
00:25:13,319 --> 00:25:18,252
I'm not sure yet, so I'll let you know this evening.

491
00:25:18,275 --> 00:25:21,010
Okay, I'll be waiting for your message.

492
00:25:21,034 --> 00:25:23,400
Will do, thanks.

493
00:25:23,423 --> 00:25:25,623
Take care.

494
00:25:25,646 --> 00:25:27,684
Excuse me.

495
00:25:27,708 --> 00:25:29,208
Scene 15: How to Choose Your Lunch Spot and Pick a Restaurant

496
00:25:29,208 --> 00:25:33,092
Where should we go for lunch today?

497
00:25:33,115 --> 00:25:35,048
It sure is.

498
00:25:35,071 --> 00:25:37,238
Any preferences?

499
00:25:37,261 --> 00:25:40,428
How about our usual spot?

500
00:25:40,451 --> 00:25:46,017
The food there is great, but it's a bit far.

501
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:48,810
Yeah, it's quite a walk.

502
00:25:48,833 --> 00:25:53,834
Plus, it's raining today, so somewhere closer would be better.

503
00:25:53,857 --> 00:25:57,943
How about the Italian place in front of the station?

504
00:25:57,967 --> 00:26:01,051
That Italian place sounds good.

505
00:26:01,075 --> 00:26:06,108
It's close to the station, the food is delicious—let's go there!

506
00:26:06,131 --> 00:26:10,767
But that place is always packed.

507
00:26:10,790 --> 00:26:16,324
It's only 11:30, so I think we'll be fine.

508
00:26:16,347 --> 00:26:17,963
It sure is.

509
00:26:17,986 --> 00:26:20,319
Let's head there early.

510
00:26:20,342 --> 00:26:23,109
What do you like from the menu?

511
00:26:23,132 --> 00:26:26,399
I love pizza.

512
00:26:26,423 --> 00:26:29,597
I always get pasta.

513
00:26:29,620 --> 00:26:36,820
Their pizzas are huge, loaded with cheese, and so good!

514
00:26:36,843 --> 00:26:39,118
They have cake too.

515
00:26:39,141 --> 00:26:41,718
Should we get dessert?

516
00:26:41,741 --> 00:26:47,419
We have a lot of work this afternoon, so let's treat ourselves to something sweet.

517
00:26:47,443 --> 00:26:49,176
That sounds good.

518
00:26:49,199 --> 00:26:51,271
I'm in!

519
00:26:51,294 --> 00:26:53,061
Should we make a reservation?

520
00:26:53,085 --> 00:26:56,286
Do you know their phone number?

521
00:26:56,309 --> 00:26:59,776
Yeah, I looked it up online.

522
00:26:59,799 --> 00:27:02,011
Then go ahead, please.

523
00:27:02,034 --> 00:27:07,168
Oh, I just checked online—they're closed today.

524
00:27:07,191 --> 00:27:10,557
Oh, that's too bad.

525
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:12,955
What should we do?

526
00:27:12,978 --> 00:27:16,312
How about the udon place next to the office?

527
00:27:16,335 --> 00:27:18,368
That sounds good.

528
00:27:18,391 --> 00:27:23,438
It's cheap, fast, and really convenient.

529
00:27:23,462 --> 00:27:26,131
And the udon is delicious too.

530
00:27:26,154 --> 00:27:29,587
Alright, let's go with udon today.

531
00:27:29,610 --> 00:27:31,988
Yes, let’s go.

532
00:27:32,012 --> 00:27:33,512
Scene 16: The New Part-Time Employee

533
00:27:33,512 --> 00:27:37,205
How's the new part-timer doing?

534
00:27:37,228 --> 00:27:39,432
Tanaka, right?

535
00:27:39,456 --> 00:27:41,691
He's really great.

536
00:27:41,714 --> 00:27:43,408
Really?

537
00:27:43,431 --> 00:27:45,598
What's he like?

538
00:27:45,621 --> 00:27:51,021
He's hardworking, kind, and just an amazing person.

539
00:27:51,044 --> 00:27:53,419
That's good to hear.

540
00:27:53,443 --> 00:27:55,676
How's his work?

541
00:27:55,699 --> 00:28:01,667
He's quick, thorough, and a huge help.

542
00:28:01,691 --> 00:28:03,744
That's impressive!

543
00:28:03,768 --> 00:28:05,901
Is he young?

544
00:28:05,924 --> 00:28:07,357
Yeah.

545
00:28:07,380 --> 00:28:09,782
He's twenty this year.

546
00:28:09,806 --> 00:28:11,973
That *is* young.

547
00:28:11,996 --> 00:28:14,162
Is he a student?

548
00:28:14,185 --> 00:28:15,919
Yeah.

549
00:28:15,941 --> 00:28:19,561
He's studying English at university.

550
00:28:19,585 --> 00:28:22,070
Does he speak English?

551
00:28:22,093 --> 00:28:23,584
Yeah.

552
00:28:23,607 --> 00:28:30,261
He speaks English and even knows some Chinese—super talented.

553
00:28:30,284 --> 00:28:34,964
That’ll be a big help when we have foreign customers.

554
00:28:34,988 --> 00:28:36,465
Yeah, for sure.

555
00:28:36,488 --> 00:28:40,171
He was even talking with an English-speaking customer yesterday.

556
00:28:40,195 --> 00:28:44,804
Is Tanaka already the shop’s favorite?

557
00:28:44,827 --> 00:28:46,261
Yeah.

558
00:28:46,284 --> 00:28:52,520
He’s cheerful, always smiling, and I think everyone likes him.

559
00:28:52,543 --> 00:28:56,755
I can’t wait to meet him soon.

560
00:28:56,779 --> 00:29:01,114
He’ll be working tomorrow afternoon.

561
00:29:01,137 --> 00:29:03,204
Alright then.

562
00:29:03,227 --> 00:29:06,427
Oh, I’m off tomorrow.

563
00:29:06,450 --> 00:29:09,216
That's too bad.

564
00:29:09,239 --> 00:29:13,239
Will he be working the day after tomorrow?

565
00:29:13,262 --> 00:29:14,699
Yeah.

566
00:29:14,722 --> 00:29:17,756
He’ll be here from the morning that day.

567
00:29:17,779 --> 00:29:19,836
Great!

568
00:29:19,859 --> 00:29:22,026
I’ll say hi to him then.

569
00:29:22,049 --> 00:29:25,533
Let’s have lunch together.

570
00:29:25,557 --> 00:29:27,362
That sounds good.

571
00:29:27,386 --> 00:29:31,386
What kind of food does he like?

572
00:29:31,409 --> 00:29:34,576
He said he likes meat.

573
00:29:34,599 --> 00:29:39,565
Then how about the hamburger steak place in front of the station?

574
00:29:39,588 --> 00:29:44,155
It’s tasty, affordable, and a great choice.

575
00:29:44,178 --> 00:29:45,864
Yeah.

576
00:29:45,887 --> 00:29:48,620
I think he’ll be happy.

577
00:29:48,643 --> 00:29:50,920
I’m looking forward to it.

578
00:29:50,944 --> 00:29:52,432
Yeah.

579
00:29:52,456 --> 00:29:55,323
I can’t wait to work with him.

580
00:29:55,346 --> 00:30:00,122
Things are going to get busier, so let’s do our best!

581
00:30:00,145 --> 00:30:01,645
Scene 17: Introducing My New Apartment

582
00:30:01,645 --> 00:30:05,612
Did you find a new place yet?

583
00:30:05,634 --> 00:30:08,634
Yes, I finally did!

584
00:30:08,657 --> 00:30:10,751
What’s it like?

585
00:30:10,775 --> 00:30:16,342
It’s close to the station, brand new, and just perfect.

586
00:30:16,365 --> 00:30:19,458
Being close to the station is so convenient.

587
00:30:19,482 --> 00:30:22,815
Yeah, it’s just a five-minute walk.

588
00:30:22,838 --> 00:30:25,926
Are there any shops nearby?

589
00:30:25,949 --> 00:30:31,916
There's a supermarket close by, as well as convenience stores—it's really convenient for shopping.

590
00:30:31,939 --> 00:30:34,472
That sounds amazing!

591
00:30:34,495 --> 00:30:37,862
Yeah, I'm really happy about it.

592
00:30:37,885 --> 00:30:40,518
Is the room spacious?

593
00:30:40,541 --> 00:30:43,112
It's reasonably spacious.

594
00:30:43,135 --> 00:30:45,269
Is the rent expensive?

595
00:30:45,292 --> 00:30:52,258
No, the rent is affordable, and the internet is free—it's a great deal!

596
00:30:52,281 --> 00:30:54,340
That’s wonderful!

597
00:30:54,363 --> 00:30:56,617
Where is it located?

598
00:30:56,641 --> 00:30:59,241
It's near Shinjuku.

599
00:30:59,264 --> 00:31:01,864
That's close to the office too, isn't it?

600
00:31:01,887 --> 00:31:05,304
Yes, it's just a 10-minute train ride.

601
00:31:05,328 --> 00:31:07,728
When are you moving?

602
00:31:07,751 --> 00:31:11,237
On the first Sunday of next month.

603
00:31:11,260 --> 00:31:13,627
Do you have a lot of stuff?

604
00:31:13,650 --> 00:31:19,823
No, I don’t have a bed or a TV—just a few things.

605
00:31:19,847 --> 00:31:22,503
Are you buying new furniture?

606
00:31:22,526 --> 00:31:27,093
Yes, I plan to go shopping this weekend.

607
00:31:27,116 --> 00:31:29,051
Need any help?

608
00:31:29,074 --> 00:31:30,885
Thank you.

609
00:31:30,908 --> 00:31:33,401
No, I’ll be fine.

610
00:31:33,425 --> 00:31:38,863
Got it. Can I come over after you move in?

611
00:31:38,886 --> 00:31:40,919
Of course!

612
00:31:40,942 --> 00:31:42,790
Please do come by!

613
00:31:42,814 --> 00:31:45,297
I’ll cook for you.

614
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:47,320
I'd love that!

615
00:31:47,343 --> 00:31:49,147
Let’s have a party!

616
00:31:49,171 --> 00:31:50,937
That sounds good.

617
00:31:50,960 --> 00:31:53,960
I’ll bring some good wine.

618
00:31:53,983 --> 00:31:56,550
I'm looking forward to it.

619
00:31:56,573 --> 00:31:58,073
Scene 18: Changing Meeting Plans Due to a Typhoon

620
00:31:58,073 --> 00:32:02,640
I’d like to discuss tomorrow’s meeting.

621
00:32:02,663 --> 00:32:05,556
Sure, what’s on your mind?

622
00:32:05,579 --> 00:32:11,832
There’s a typhoon coming tomorrow, so trains might be suspended.

623
00:32:11,855 --> 00:32:14,347
I saw the news.

624
00:32:14,371 --> 00:32:17,588
It looks like a big one.

625
00:32:17,612 --> 00:32:21,679
Yes, they say it’s very dangerous.

626
00:32:21,702 --> 00:32:24,991
Commuting to the office will be tough.

627
00:32:25,014 --> 00:32:30,687
How about we move the meeting online?

628
00:32:30,711 --> 00:32:33,278
Online, you mean?

629
00:32:33,300 --> 00:32:35,434
That sounds good.

630
00:32:35,457 --> 00:32:40,460
Everyone can join from home, so it’s safer.

631
00:32:40,483 --> 00:32:42,129
It sure is.

632
00:32:42,152 --> 00:32:45,085
We shouldn’t take any risks.

633
00:32:45,108 --> 00:32:46,842
Thank you.

634
00:32:46,865 --> 00:32:50,721
The meeting is still at 2 PM, right?

635
00:32:50,744 --> 00:32:54,358
Yes, the time remains the same.

636
00:32:54,381 --> 00:32:56,114
Alright.

637
00:32:56,137 --> 00:32:58,871
What about the materials?

638
00:32:58,894 --> 00:33:03,331
I’ll email them to everyone this evening.

639
00:33:03,354 --> 00:33:07,688
I’ll read them before the meeting—thanks in advance!

640
00:33:07,711 --> 00:33:11,677
Should we inform the manager as well?

641
00:33:11,700 --> 00:33:17,519
Yes, I’ll let the manager know—don’t worry.

642
00:33:17,543 --> 00:33:19,143
Thank you.

643
00:33:19,166 --> 00:33:20,844
That would be a huge help.

644
00:33:20,867 --> 00:33:25,001
Weren’t there any client appointments?

645
00:33:25,024 --> 00:33:29,957
Yes, there was one scheduled for tomorrow morning.

646
00:33:29,980 --> 00:33:32,313
Did you cancel it?

647
00:33:32,336 --> 00:33:38,070
Yes, since the rain is heavy, we rescheduled it for next week.

648
00:33:38,093 --> 00:33:40,359
That's great to hear.

649
00:33:40,382 --> 00:33:45,077
I'll be working from home all day tomorrow.

650
00:33:45,101 --> 00:33:47,916
Are you taking your laptop home?

651
00:33:47,939 --> 00:33:53,232
Yes, it's heavy, but I need it, so I'll take it.

652
00:33:53,256 --> 00:33:55,722
Please get home safely.

653
00:33:55,745 --> 00:33:59,920
Yes, I'll head home before the wind gets too strong.

654
00:33:59,944 --> 00:34:03,517
Let's wrap up work early today.

655
00:34:03,541 --> 00:34:05,589
Sounds good, thank you.

656
00:34:05,612 --> 00:34:08,021
Good morning.

657
00:34:08,045 --> 00:34:09,545
Scene 19: Dealing with a Broken Computer

658
00:34:09,545 --> 00:34:11,778
Good morning.

659
00:34:11,801 --> 00:34:14,134
Good morning.

660
00:34:14,157 --> 00:34:16,490
What happened?

661
00:34:16,513 --> 00:34:18,513
I'm sorry about this.

662
00:34:18,536 --> 00:34:22,210
My computer just broke.

663
00:34:22,234 --> 00:34:23,967
What?

664
00:34:23,990 --> 00:34:25,857
Really?

665
00:34:25,881 --> 00:34:27,647
Yeah.

666
00:34:27,670 --> 00:34:31,670
The screen's been completely black since this morning.

667
00:34:31,693 --> 00:34:34,627
That's rough.

668
00:34:34,650 --> 00:34:37,583
Does it turn on at all?

669
00:34:37,606 --> 00:34:42,614
It powers on, but I can't see anything.

670
00:34:42,637 --> 00:34:45,074
That's rough.

671
00:34:45,098 --> 00:34:50,101
What about today's presentation materials?

672
00:34:50,124 --> 00:34:55,991
They're on that computer, so I can't access them right now.

673
00:34:56,014 --> 00:34:59,347
Didn't you save them to a USB?

674
00:34:59,370 --> 00:35:04,854
I usually do, but I forgot yesterday.

675
00:35:04,878 --> 00:35:07,316
Alright then.

676
00:35:07,339 --> 00:35:10,942
The meeting is this afternoon, right?

677
00:35:10,966 --> 00:35:12,647
Yeah.

678
00:35:12,671 --> 00:35:15,471
I'm really sorry about this.

679
00:35:15,493 --> 00:35:19,900
We still have time, so it'll be fine.

680
00:35:19,924 --> 00:35:21,591
Thank you.

681
00:35:21,614 --> 00:35:25,792
Want to use my old laptop?

682
00:35:25,815 --> 00:35:27,068
Yeah.

683
00:35:27,092 --> 00:35:29,325
Could you lend it to me?

684
00:35:29,348 --> 00:35:31,548
Sure, no problem.

685
00:35:31,571 --> 00:35:33,847
I'll bring it right away.

686
00:35:33,870 --> 00:35:35,504
Please.

687
00:35:35,527 --> 00:35:40,060
I'll quickly redo the materials.

688
00:35:40,083 --> 00:35:43,849
I'll help, so let's do it together.

689
00:35:43,872 --> 00:35:46,476
Thank you so much.

690
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:50,467
Are you sending the broken laptop for repairs?

691
00:35:50,490 --> 00:35:52,023
Yeah.

692
00:35:52,046 --> 00:35:56,328
I'll have the company's IT department take a look.

693
00:35:56,352 --> 00:35:59,318
That's a good idea.

694
00:35:59,341 --> 00:36:02,948
I hope the data isn't lost.

695
00:36:02,972 --> 00:36:07,505
There's a lot of important data, so I'm worried.

696
00:36:07,528 --> 00:36:09,097
Yeah.

697
00:36:09,121 --> 00:36:12,654
I'll be more careful about saving from now on.

698
00:36:12,677 --> 00:36:17,334
Everyone makes mistakes, so don't worry about it.

699
00:36:17,358 --> 00:36:20,491
Thanks for your concern.

700
00:36:20,514 --> 00:36:24,781
Alright, let's finish the materials quickly.

701
00:36:24,804 --> 00:36:26,175
Yeah.

702
00:36:26,198 --> 00:36:28,053
I'll do my best.

703
00:36:28,076 --> 00:36:29,576
Scene 20: Weekend Fun at the Amusement Park

704
00:36:29,576 --> 00:36:34,344
Did you do anything fun over the weekend?

705
00:36:34,368 --> 00:36:38,539
Yes, I went to an amusement park with friends.

706
00:36:38,563 --> 00:36:40,445
That sounds good.

707
00:36:40,468 --> 00:36:43,072
The weather was perfect, wasn't it?

708
00:36:43,096 --> 00:36:49,179
Yeah, it was warm and there was no wind—it was amazing.

709
00:36:49,202 --> 00:36:52,135
Did you ride the roller coaster?

710
00:36:52,158 --> 00:36:53,635
Yeah.

711
00:36:53,659 --> 00:36:58,192
It's scary but fun, so I rode it three times!

712
00:36:58,215 --> 00:37:00,382
Three times?

713
00:37:00,405 --> 00:37:02,405
That's impressive!

714
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:07,713
My friend loves roller coasters, so I rode with them.

715
00:37:07,736 --> 00:37:10,302
Was it crowded?

716
00:37:10,325 --> 00:37:11,892
Yeah.

717
00:37:11,915 --> 00:37:17,248
What about today's presentation materials?

718
00:37:17,271 --> 00:37:19,328
They're on that computer, so I can't access them right now.

719
00:37:19,352 --> 00:37:23,560
I walked so much that my feet are sore.

720
00:37:23,583 --> 00:37:25,816
You must be exhausted.

721
00:37:25,839 --> 00:37:29,406
I've been staying home the whole time.

722
00:37:29,429 --> 00:37:32,286
The meeting is this afternoon, right?

723
00:37:32,310 --> 00:37:38,077
I wanted to clean and read some books, so I didn’t go out.

724
00:37:38,100 --> 00:37:41,233
Did you get some good rest?

725
00:37:41,256 --> 00:37:44,667
I slept well, so I feel great today.

726
00:37:44,690 --> 00:37:46,664
That's good to hear.

727
00:37:46,687 --> 00:37:49,354
What kind of book did you read?

728
00:37:49,377 --> 00:37:52,177
A book on Japanese history.

729
00:37:52,200 --> 00:37:54,433
Isn’t it too difficult?

730
00:37:54,456 --> 00:38:00,105
It’s a little tough because of all the kanji, but it’s really interesting.

731
00:38:00,129 --> 00:38:02,462
That’s a great way to learn.

732
00:38:02,485 --> 00:38:03,704
Yeah.

733
00:38:03,728 --> 00:38:08,166
I want to improve my Japanese, so I’ll keep at it.

734
00:38:08,189 --> 00:38:10,209
That’s wonderful!

735
00:38:10,232 --> 00:38:15,043
How about visiting an art museum together on your next day off?

736
00:38:15,067 --> 00:38:17,340
An art museum?

737
00:38:17,363 --> 00:38:21,630
There’s a famous painting on display, and I’d love to see it.

738
00:38:21,653 --> 00:38:23,268
That sounds good.

739
00:38:23,292 --> 00:38:27,625
I love looking at art too, so I’d love to go.

740
00:38:27,648 --> 00:38:30,815
How about Sunday, then?

741
00:38:30,838 --> 00:38:33,977
The one near the station, right?

742
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:35,467
Yeah.

743
00:38:35,490 --> 00:38:39,823
It’s close, beautiful, and just a wonderful place.

744
00:38:39,846 --> 00:38:42,257
I'm looking forward to it.